    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11478" root="خمر" body-key="x">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَمْرَةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَمْرٌ</span>, in two places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also, (S, A,
K,) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خِمْرَةٌ</span></b>  (Kr, K) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خُمْرَةٌ</span></b> , (K,) The
<i>odour</i> of perfume: (S, A:) or <i>a sweet odour:</i>
(K:) and the last signifies also <i>an odour which
has infected</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَامَرَ</span>, i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَالَطَ</span>,) <i>a person;</i> (K;)
as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَمَرَةٌ</span></b> . (AZ, K.) You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَجَدْتُ خَمْرَةَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الطِّيبِ</span> <i>I experienced,</i> or <i>smelt, the odour of the
perfume.</i> (S, A.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَمَرٌ</span>, in two places.

